{
  "id": "V18",
  "title": "Wind and seismic together",
  "intent": "Load type \"both\" on two single-wall lines: Line A where seismic governs the sheathing and Line B where wind governs. Checks the wind ASD unit shear 0.6W against the wind capacity column, the wind combinations D + 0.6W, 0.6D + 0.6W and D + 0.75(0.6W) + 0.75Lr for the end forces, the governing load type per wall, and the service wind deflection with α_s (report only).",
  "covers": [
    "SDPWS 2021 Table 4.3A wind column",
    "ASCE 7-22 §2.4.1 (5)–(7)",
    "Governing E vs W",
    "α_s wind deflection (report only)"
  ],
  "handCalc": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "text": "Gravity on each 10 ft wall: self-weight 10 psf × 10 × 10 = 1.00 k + D 100 plf × 10 ft = 1.00 k → D = 2.00 k, R_D = 1.00 k each end; Lr 60 plf × 10 = 0.60 k → R_Lr = 0.30 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "text": "Line A SW-1 (1.0E = 5 k, 1.0W = 6 k): v_E = 0.7 × 5 × 1000 / 10 = 350.00 plf, v_W = 0.6 × 6 × 1000 / 10 = 360.00 plf. Lightest pattern with v_E ≤ seismic column and v_W ≤ wind column (wind = 1.4 × seismic, SDPWS 4.3.3): 4\" o.c. (470 / 658 plf). D/C E = 0.745, W = 0.547 → seismic governs."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "text": "Line A SW-1 (1.0E = 5 k, 1.0W = 6 k) end forces: N_E = 5 × 10/10 = 5.00 k, N_W = 6.00 k; R_D = 1.00, R_Lr = 0.30 k. Uplift: (0.6−0.14S_DS)D + 0.7E = 3.040 k, 0.6D + 0.6W = 0.6 × 6.00 − 0.6 × 1.00 = 3.000 k → T = 3.040 k → HDUE3. Compression: (1+0.14S_DS)D + 0.7E = 4.640, D + 0.6W = 1.00 + 0.6 × 6.00 = 4.600, D + 0.75(0.6W) + 0.75Lr = 3.925 → C = 4.640 k → (2)2x4."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "text": "Line B SW-2 (1.0E = 2 k, 1.0W = 12 k): v_E = 0.7 × 2 × 1000 / 10 = 140.00 plf, v_W = 0.6 × 12 × 1000 / 10 = 720.00 plf. Lightest pattern with v_E ≤ seismic column and v_W ≤ wind column (wind = 1.4 × seismic, SDPWS 4.3.3): 3\" o.c. (611 / 856 plf). D/C E = 0.229, W = 0.841 → wind governs."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "text": "Line B SW-2 (1.0E = 2 k, 1.0W = 12 k) end forces: N_E = 2 × 10/10 = 2.00 k, N_W = 12.00 k; R_D = 1.00, R_Lr = 0.30 k. Uplift: (0.6−0.14S_DS)D + 0.7E = 0.940 k, 0.6D + 0.6W = 0.6 × 12.00 − 0.6 × 1.00 = 6.600 k → T = 6.600 k → HDUE7. Compression: (1+0.14S_DS)D + 0.7E = 2.540, D + 0.6W = 1.00 + 0.6 × 12.00 = 8.200, D + 0.75(0.6W) + 0.75Lr = 6.625 → C = 8.200 k → 6x4."
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "text": "SW-2 end post: 6x4 at 10 ft: F_c* = 2640 psi, F_cE = 496 psi, C_P = 0.1799 → cap = 9.14 k ≥ 8.200 k (lighter posts in the list order are below 8.200 k or below the HDUE7 minimum post)."
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "text": "SW-2 service wind deflection with α_s = 0.7: v = 840.00 plf, T = C = α_s·N_W = 8400.00 lb (lateral only), A = 19.25 in², G_a = 22 → 8vh³/(EAb) = 0.0205, vh/(1000G_a) = 0.3818, Δ_HD = δ_LRFD × T / T_LRFD of HDUE7 = 0.216 × 8400.00 / 9821 = 0.1847, r = 0.6982 → Δ_c = 0.0191, h·Δa/b = 0.2039 → δ = 0.6062 in; δ/h_sx = 0.6062 / 120 = 0.0051 (report only, no limit)."
    },
    {
      "step": 8,
      "text": "Line checks G1–G12 pass on both lines (1.0W and 1.0E balance; gravity all to the foundation)."
    },
    {
      "step": 9,
      "text": "Seismic drift, Line A (1.0E = 5 k): SW-1 (Eq. 4.3-1, → governs): v = 1000 × 5.000 / 10 = 500.00 plf, A = 10.5 in², G_a = 20 k/in → 8vh³/(EAb) = 0.0224; vh/(1000G_a) = 0.2500; uplift end T = 5000.00 lb (lateral); Δ_HD = δ_LRFD × T / T_LRFD = 0.178 × 5000.00 / 5306 = 0.1677 (HDUE3); r = 5000.00 / (10.5 × 625) = 0.7619 → Δ_c = 0.0224; h·Δa/b = 10 × (0.1677 + 0.0224) / 10 = 0.1901 → δ = 0.4625 in. Story drift Level 1: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-1 0.4625 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.4625 / 1.0 = 1.850 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 10 × 12 = 2.400 in → OK."
    },
    {
      "step": 10,
      "text": "Seismic drift, Line B (1.0E = 2 k): SW-2 (Eq. 4.3-1, → governs): v = 1000 × 2.000 / 10 = 200.00 plf, A = 19.25 in², G_a = 22 k/in → 8vh³/(EAb) = 0.0049; vh/(1000G_a) = 0.0909; uplift end T = 2000.00 lb (lateral); Δ_HD = δ_LRFD × T / T_LRFD = 0.216 × 2000.00 / 9821 = 0.0440 (HDUE7); r = 2000.00 / (19.25 × 625) = 0.1662 → Δ_c = 0.0046; h·Δa/b = 10 × (0.0440 + 0.0046) / 10 = 0.0485 → δ = 0.1443 in. Story drift Level 1: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-2 0.1443 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.1443 / 1.0 = 0.577 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 10 × 12 = 2.400 in → OK."
    }
  ],
